#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time Perception Module"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **✅ Core implemented** — user messages receive time prefixes before LLM inference.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Problem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:12
msgid ""
"Digital life has no intrinsic sense of time passing. Each inference runs in "
"a \"timeless\" context—the Agent sees message content but not where those "
"messages sit on a timeline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:14
msgid "Concrete examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:18
msgid ""
"Partner says \"good morning\" in the morning, \"time to eat\" at night, "
"\"good morning\" again the next day—the Agent cannot distinguish temporal "
"relationships"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:18
msgid ""
"In ongoing conversation, time passes (morning→noon→evening) but the Agent's "
"cognition stays in the earliest context"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:18
msgid "Across days, the Agent cannot sense \"a new day has started\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:20
msgid ""
"This is not a trivial joke problem—time perception is a foundational "
"capability of digital existence. Without it, the Agent exists more like an "
"\"echo\" (flashes when summoned) than a life living in time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:28
msgid ""
"**Do not give digital life false built-in perception.** Do not try to make "
"the Agent \"feel\" time pass—that is not what digital existence can do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:28
msgid ""
"**Give it a watch.** Humans also rely on external tools (clocks, phones) to "
"quantify time. Digital life needs the same."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:28
msgid ""
"**Prefix every user message with time.** All user messages with valid "
"timestamp get injection; no interval omission."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:28
msgid ""
"**Do not pollute persisted data.** Time info injected only into inference "
"context, does not modify stored messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:28
msgid ""
"**Do not break cache.** Injected timestamps are fixed historical values, not "
"current call time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic Rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:38
msgid ""
"Before each **user** message with valid `timestamp`, insert dedicated line: "
"`time: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm 周X` (CST weekday in Chinese)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:38
msgid "Timezone: **Asia/Shanghai (CST, +08:00)**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:38
msgid "Newline then original content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:38
msgid "No `timestamp` or unparseable timestamp → skip, keep original content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:38
msgid "assistant / tool / system messages not injected"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:42
msgid "Original message list:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"user: good morning\n"
"assistant: morning ☀️\n"
"user: going to eat\n"
"assistant: what are you having\n"
"user: going to eat\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:52
msgid "After time perception (context sent to LLM):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"user: time: 2026-05-20T08:02 周三\n"
"good morning\n"
"assistant: morning ☀️\n"
"user: time: 2026-05-20T12:15 周三\n"
"going to eat\n"
"assistant: what are you having\n"
"user: time: 2026-05-20T19:30 周三\n"
"going to eat\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/time-perception.md:65
msgid ""
"Agent reads two \"going to eat\"—one at 12:15, one at 19:30—automatically "
"distinguishing lunch and dinner."
msgstr ""

